                <pb facs="0879" n="1713" xml:id="pg1713"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/2023a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Willard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-26T19:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 26, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1736. For Chadbourne [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 337. War Trade Board on suggestion of General Pershing has authorized
                    McFadden to put himself at disposal of A.E.F. in undertaking the purchase of
                    horses and mules in Spain. McFadden is advised that War Trade Board is prepared
                    to support him fully either in exerting economic pressure upon Spain, or in
                    granting concessions to Spain, as may seem best, and that it is prepared to take
                    up the matter of securing vigorous and joint representation to Spain by
                    Ambassadors there of Associated Governments. We are confident that McFadden will
                    be much aided by the cooperation of your organization, which we have advised he
                    may confidently rely on.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
